P-10 (spec 017, the night shift; plan.md §10, Q13; tasks.md T071): the night shift's settings layers, prompts, and
image pins trigger the agent-config evals, as .claude/ and the devcontainer's Claude Code pin do.

What it changes:
  - tools/gates/gate: the agent-config-evals step is triggered by a branch that touches deploy/night-shift/claude/,
    deploy/night-shift/runner/prompts/, or deploy/night-shift/images/pins.json (which names the Claude Code every night
    session runs), beside CLAUDE.md, REVIEW.md, .claude/, and the Claude Code pin; its docstring and its SKIP line name
    them. The runner's code, the container specs, and the Dockerfiles stay code (make test holds them).
  - evals/agent-config/behavioral.py: TRIGGER_PATHS gains the same three, so the trigger hash covers them. Without
    this, a branch that changed only a prompt would hash as main does, and main's attested run would pass it: the
    trigger would be hollow. Paths that don't exist add nothing to the hash, so main's hash doesn't move until the
    night shift's files are on main; from then on, the first make evals-agent-config after that merge records it.
  - tools/gates/test/test_gate.py: three parametrize cases (a settings layer, a prompt, pins.json: PENDING until a run
    exists), a SKIP test for night.py, a container spec, a Dockerfile, and a neighbour folder, and a "triggered by"
    test.
  - evals/agent-config/test_behavioral.py: the hash covers a prompt, a settings layer, and pins.json (and a change to
    its pin), not night.py, a spec, or a Dockerfile; an export hashes as the work tree does.
behavioral.py is in evals/agent-config/, also human-only; it's here because the gate's trigger and the hash must name
the same paths.

Spec IDs: the Assumptions' named deviation "Agent configuration outside .claude/" ("P-10 adds it to the gate's
agent-configuration trigger, so a change there runs the same evals"), Q13.

Needed for: the merge.

How to apply, on your own branch, from the repository's root (one line each):
  B=feat/017-g5-patches
  F=docs/merge-requests/2026-11-12-feat-017-p10.patch
  git show "refs/heads/$B:$F" > /tmp/p10.patch
  sha256sum /tmp/p10.patch
  patch -p1 --dry-run < /tmp/p10.patch
  patch -p1 < /tmp/p10.patch

Verified on a fresh `git archive refs/heads/main` export (main d4870ec8): dry run and apply clean; ruff check and
ruff format clean on the four files; `pytest tools/gates/test/test_gate.py evals/agent-config/`: 590 passed in 244 s.

